we just want to bring you some words  from the Prime Minister Rishi sunak has  been speaking at a school in South  London this week no doubt informing them  all about his plans to make them Carry  On Learning maths until the age of 18  but he's been taking some questions  including one on the emergency  anti-strike legislation that the  government announced yesterday afternoon  let's have a listen to what he said  well first of all it's great to be here  at Harris Battersea this morning talking  to some of the amazing teachers and  fantastic students all the opportunities  that I've had in my life began with the  fact that I was fortunate to receive an  amazing education it's one of the most  important reasons I got into politics  was to ensure that every one of our  children has a brilliant education  that's why we invested billions pound  more in schools in the Autumn statement  but we've got to keep going because  every child deserves a fantastic  education it's one of the most powerful  things we can do for them in our country  and that's what the government's  priority is you know with regard to  strikes you know yesterday the  government wrote to all union leaders  inviting them in for talks on Monday you  know incredibly value the important work  that our public sector workers do  especially our nurses and we want to  have an honest grown-up conversation  about what's affordable what's  responsible for the country those  invitations have gone out and I'm  hopeful that those meetings can happen  on Monday so we can have a productive of  conversation and find a way through this  and just on the legislation that you  brought in could people be sacked for  not going to work in the Health Service  so you know I I fully believe in the  Union's role in our society and the  freedom for them to strike but I also  believe that that should be balanced  with the right of ordinary working  people to go about their lives free from  significant disruption and that's why  we're going to bring forward new laws in  common with countries like France Italy  Spain and others that ensure that we  have minimum levels of safety in  critical areas like fire like ambulance  so that even when strikes are going on  you know that your health will be  protected I think that's entirely  reasonable and that's what our new laws  will do when it comes to the current  industrial action being taken by nurses  they've indicated that they might be  willing to settle for 10 could you go a  bit further with your payoff could you  meet them halfway and we've always been  clear that we want to have a grown-up  honest conversation a two-way  conversation with union leaders and  that's why the government has written  all departments have written to all  their unions inviting them in for talks  on Monday so that we can have those  conversations talking about what's  affordable what's reasonable what's  responsible for our country I think  everyone agrees that the most pressing  economic priority we have is reducing  the cost of living and getting a grip of  inflation is the best way we can do that  to ease the cost of living not only for  nurses but for everyone and that's why  earlier this week I made five promises  about what I wanted to do and that was  to halve inflation grow the economy  reduce debt cut waiting lists and stop  the boats will those talks that you're  talking about inviting unions in for  include talks about this year's pay so  what we do is what we've said is we want  to have a grown-up honest conversation  with all union leaders about what is  responsible what is reasonable and what  is Affordable for our country when it  comes to pay we think that those  conversations should happen that's why  we've invited everyone in to have those  talks on Monday and I'm hopeful that  those talks will be constructive and we  can find a way through this beyond the  industrial and rest in the wider NHS  there is a crisis people are we don't  know how many but people are almost  certainly unnecessarily dying does that  trouble you the NHS is obviously under  enormous pressure as we recover from  covid and I have enormous admiration for  all the people working incredibly hard  in the NHS right now to help get us  through that now we are supporting them  with billions of pounds of extra funding  but in particular this winter what we  want to do is make sure that we move  people out of hospitals into social care  into communities that's one of the most  powerful ways we can ease some of the  pressures on a e departments and  ambulances that are waiting too long if  we can move people into social care  that's why we've put money into doing  that we need to make sure that money  reaches the front line and makes a  difference and there's various other  initiatives that we're rolling out that  will also help ease some of the burdens  but people should rest assured you know  one of my promises that I made this week  was to tackle NHS weights and I'm fully  committed to doing that we're putting  the extra money in and we need to make  sure that the initiatives that we've put  in place actually make a difference but  this is what I'm focused on I've set out  five promises for the country three this  week to halve inflation reduce debt cut  waiting lists stop the boats grow the  economy that's what I'm prioritizing  you spoke also in your speech earlier  this week about the importance of family  and you spoke about how important your  family is to you how do you feel then  when you see the royal family being so  publicly torn apart  I think as you would expect it's not  appropriate for me to comment on matters  to do with the Royal Family  more broadly Prince Harry has talked  about the number of Taliban fighters he  believed he killed in Afghanistan just  on the point about military personnel  talking about the number of people they  believe they have killed is that wise  does that create a security risk for  anyone who's been in the forces you know  again I wouldn't comment on matters to  do with the royal family I would just  say I'm enormously grateful to our Armed  Forces for the incredible job they do in  keeping us all safe we're all very  fortunate for their service
 

